Sure! To update a break node’s label to `'loopEnd'` (but only if it isn’t already `'loopEnd'`), you can use the `updateBreak` function like this:

```javascript
// Assume you have the break node in string form, e.g.:
const nodeStr = '{"type":"BreakStatement","label":"currentLabel"}';

// Call the function
const result = updateBreak({
  node: nodeStr,
  label: 'loopEnd'
});

console.log(result);
```

If you already have the node object instead of a string, just stringify it before passing it to the function. Let me know if you’d like help converting your specific node or if you need the function to check the current label first!
